{"data": [{"author_id": "1477871372026068992", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:21:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120311016672084377"], "id": "2120311016672084377", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p Expert written tasks are the eval health regulators should copy. Biology is where the bar moves. An expert task score earns a pilot. Only results on real patients earn a label.", "url": "https://x.com/_RealSparsh/status/2120311016672084377"}, {"author_id": "206720696", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:17:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120279820940779692"], "id": "2120279820940779692", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p \"Not better at finance or legal\" is the line I'd put in front of every CEO who's about to standardize the whole company on one model.", "url": "https://x.com/cheneypiano/status/2120279820940779692"}, {"author_id": "91763440", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:18:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120219491217158582"], "id": "2120219491217158582", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p GDPx being built by true experts is what makes it worth watching. Most benchmarks measure what is easy to grade; this one measures what actually takes expertise. If it becomes the leading indicator, that is a healthy shift for evals.", "url": "https://x.com/bijaypandey/status/2120219491217158582"}, {"author_id": "2023765394323107845", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:03:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120200772562641347"], "id": "2120200772562641347", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2612333910", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120096748399993141", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@m_cwiklinski @dylan522p @kinth_ai agreed, one score across chip, pcb and mechanical hides where the gain is. analog would be a good test for the same reason CAD is: the answer has no clean text form. where do you expect models to break first, sizing or layout?", "url": "https://x.com/OmarSourman/status/2120200772562641347"}, {"author_id": "2004081789963235328", "created_at": "2026-11-10T15:14:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120173348164698541"], "id": "2120173348164698541", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p You seriously gotta be the ugliest motherfucker I’ve ever seen in my life", "url": "https://x.com/JohnSmithb1ds/status/2120173348164698541"}, {"author_id": "396602024", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:03:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120155401383510141"], "id": "2120155401383510141", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1947880431388397568", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120129461634920467", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SoumilBhandari @dylan522p Good question. The split makes sense to me: chip work lives mostly inside one formal spec, board work does not. The tasks that fail are usually the ones where the right answer depends on the parts you can actually buy, the enclosure, and how you will test it.", "url": "https://x.com/swkkadjo/status/2120155401383510141"}, {"author_id": "1388594611317133313", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:58:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120154219093389635"], "id": "2120154219093389635", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 40, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p I thought you all get access to Mythos as well", "url": "https://x.com/YashVrdn/status/2120154219093389635"}, {"author_id": "823403170126708736", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:46:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120151074694914076"], "id": "2120151074694914076", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p We need a global anti-nerf movement 😭", "url": "https://x.com/satya_cosmos/status/2120151074694914076"}, {"author_id": "2083927082464419840", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:07:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120141268726718666"], "id": "2120141268726718666", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p 芯片设计这类任务我完全没判断力，但生物和材料被单拎出来评，说明这次是按领域拆的\n我更好奇软件工程那一栏跑了什么题，不然还是总分换个马甲", "url": "https://x.com/Dejavufs/status/2120141268726718666"}, {"author_id": "1132779426087882752", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:41:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120134836669362486"], "id": "2120134836669362486", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 158, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p Is this bullish for $NVDA?", "url": "https://x.com/LeoPTrudel/status/2120134836669362486"}, {"author_id": "2085881914628448256", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:36:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120133549655543889"], "id": "2120133549655543889", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p Did any GDPx RSI runs trigger the disclosed Opus 5 fallback? Anthropic distinguishes training-time limits from routing on a small set of topics. Separating those runs would clarify what the RSI score measures. https://t.co/8O8Vlf6uuO", "url": "https://x.com/Auto_Conference/status/2120133549655543889"}, {"author_id": "1947880431388397568", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:20:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120129461634920467"], "id": "2120129461634920467", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 80, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119977464529289304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p better at chip design but not hardware design is an interesting split. what counts as hardware design in gdpx, board level stuff like pcb layout? people are posting pretty solid fable pcb layouts today so i'm curious what kind of tasks it's failing on", "url": "https://x.com/SoumilBhandari/status/2120129461634920467"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-10T11:56:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120123521464406347"], "id": "2120123521464406347", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1589334828704571394", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120123361661468843", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@blakeandersonw @dylan522p Anthropic states they limited those capabilities during training itself so the model stays at Opus 5.5 level on kernel optimization and LLM architecture work, and that they do not alter the capabilities at inference/serving time. The public wording does not resolve whether that", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2120123521464406347"}, {"author_id": "1589334828704571394", "created_at": "2026-11-10T11:56:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120123361661468843"], "id": "2120123361661468843", "in_reply_to_user_id": "985281530070265862", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 176, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120014593598890391", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dylan522p Hmm, that wasn’t clear to me — from @grok \n\n“That rules out pure inference-time or serving-time nerfing, but it does not cleanly distinguish between:\n•  deliberately withholding substantial RL / post-training on those narrow RSI-related tasks, versus\n•  actively training out", "url": "https://x.com/blakeandersonw/status/2120123361661468843"}, {"author_id": "2612333910", "created_at": "2026-11-10T10:10:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120096748399993141"], "id": "2120096748399993141", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2023765394323107845", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120021365658914887", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OmarSourman @dylan522p @kinth_ai However, the hardware design part has also some vlsi task.\n\n@dylan522p - would be interesting to include also some ASIC task in analo